# TASK-056 — TopAppBar.diff
# Fix: Conditional snippet prop → {#if} wrap pattern

## PROBLEM
Line 58 (old):
  leading={showBack ? backBtn : undefined}

This conditional snippet prop causes HMR crash:
- Symbol(hmr anchor) is tied to the snippet reference
- When showBack toggles, the snippet changes between `backBtn` and `undefined`
- Svelte 5 HMR cannot reconcile the snapshot diff → crashes with "Symbol(hmr anchor)" error

## FIX
Replace conditional snippet prop with {#if} wrapper — two separate Nav instances:

--- OLD (lines 55-60)
<Nav
	position="top"
	title={title}
	leading={showBack ? backBtn : undefined}
	ariaLabel="Top navigation"
/>

--- NEW (lines 55-68)
{#if showBack}
	<Nav
		position="top"
		title={title}
		leading={backBtn}
		ariaLabel="Top navigation"
	/>
{:else}
	<Nav
		position="top"
		title={title}
		ariaLabel="Top navigation"
	/>
{/if}

## RATIONALE
- Each Nav instance has a STABLE set of props (no conditional snippet)
- showBack toggle causes full Nav instance swap (mounted/unmounted) instead of prop-level snippet change
- HMR anchor per Nav instance is stable — no Symbol(hmr anchor) collision
- Nav.svelte guard `{#if leading}` never sees a stale/broken snippet reference
